prompt:
A real photograph of the ground-floor landing of an old apartment building in the Graça district of Lisbon on a September evening, in a tall vertical picture, caught as it happens, as a visitor would take it with a good phone camera. Taken with a 24 mm lens at standing eye height from the open street door, looking into the landing and up the first flight of the wooden stairs, everything in sharp focus. Warm light from a glass lamp hanging from the ceiling and the last daylight from a small window on the stairs; the textures of real glazed tiles, worn wood, painted plaster, wrought iron, cotton, denim and skin.

The first reference picture shows the young man from the front, the second shows him from his side: his face, his wavy dark-brown hair, his short stubble, his build, his height and his clothes, the royal-blue hooded sweatshirt with its red band across the chest, the white t-shirt, the cream scarf with small blue embroidered flowers, the dark-blue jeans and the white canvas sneakers, stay exactly as in them.

Every surface in the picture is plain: the wall tiles are plain glazed squares in green and white, the doors are plain painted wood, the mat is plain brown, and the clothes are plain cloth. Each object stands clearly on its own, with a band of bare floor or bare wall around it, so that the eye can tell at once where everything is.

The picture is built in three bands, from the bottom edge to the top edge.

THE FOREGROUND, along the bottom of the picture:
- the young man of the reference pictures stands on the left of the middle, seen whole from his head to his white sneakers, which stand on the worn red-tiled floor with their soft shadow beside them; his body is turned in three-quarter view towards the right of the picture; he bows his head politely, a little too low, both hands holding the handle of his bright grass-green hard-shell suitcase, which stands upright on its wheels in front of his knees;
- on the floor in front of the open apartment door on the right, a plain brown doormat;
- on the left edge of the picture, a small wooden chair with a straw seat, and a white cat asleep on it.

THE MIDDLE OF THE LANDING, from left to right:
- the back wall is covered in plain green and white glazed tiles up to shoulder height, plain white plaster above;
- in the centre, the first flight of narrow wooden stairs rises towards the left, with a dark wrought-iron handrail and worn wooden steps;
- on the right, the open green door of the ground-floor apartment, with a small brass doorbell beside it and a key in its lock; in the doorway stands the landlady, a small round woman of seventy with short white hair, in a dark-blue dress and a plain apron printed with large red flowers, holding up a little white birdcage in both hands with great ceremony, as if she were introducing a member of the family; inside the cage, a yellow canary sits on its perch, its beak open in song; she smiles proudly at the young man;
- on the wall beside her door, a row of four small grey metal letter boxes.

THE UPPER PART OF THE PICTURE, across the upper third:
- the stairs turn at a small landing, where a small window with a white wooden frame shows the pink evening sky and a red-tiled roof across the street;
- on the windowsill, a terracotta flower pot with red geraniums;
- on the plaster wall of the stairs, a small framed picture of a white church;
- from the ceiling, a round frosted glass lamp on a short brass chain gives a warm light.

The landing is small, tidy and calm: between the objects and the people, the same bare red-tiled floor and the same bare walls.
